      "supported_claims": [
        "Root source license is Apache2.0; this does not settle all dependency rights.",
        "Python>=3.12; Beta classifier; broad runtime ranges are declarations rather than a resolved environment.",
        "Default test configuration excludes correctness and nightly markers.",
        "Pinned source declares1.0.0rc1, distinct from previously saved PyPI0.9.0 metadata.",
        "Constructs a finite-epsilon upper-treated minus lower-control prediction contrast.",
        "Above-cutoff treatment rule is explicit; input validation checks dummy coding but the selected method does not prove design validity.",
        "Donut/bandwidth masks and small-sample warning are distinct from identifying assumptions.",
        "Selected Bayesian plotting path uses equal-tail posterior quantiles.",
        "Linear model has Normal coefficient priors and Normal likelihood with HalfNormal noise prior.",
        "Sampling merges explicit overrides; dependency declarations alone do not fix sampler behavior.",
        "mu and y_hat have different meanings.",
        "PyMC adapter extracts mu; sklearn points acquire singleton chain/draw axes without inferential uncertainty.",
        "Fresh model resets result state; a frozen design fingerprint does not detect later data edits; changed data require a new experiment.",
        "Formula design metadata are part of the experiment contract, not a causal-design certificate.",
        "Point-estimation interface differs from Bayesian sampling; no RD-specific coverage result inferred.",
        "Selected tests inspect RD fit/type/plot paths; not an executed target-recovery result here.",
        "Source tests cover selected integer/bool conversion and mask behavior; not executed in this review.",
        "Selected recovery examples concern other designs; no RD recovery test found by this literal search."
      ],
